Phase 1: Create Custom IAM Roles

📝 Custom roles give you fine-grained permissions tailored to your org. You said "new roles" — I suggest these:
Role 	Suggested Permissions 	Purpose
sl_platform_admin 	compute., container., iam.serviceAccounts.actAs 	Administer GKE and compute resources
sl_security_admin 	iam., orgpolicy., logging., monitoring. 	Manage security policies and audit
sl_developer 	resourcemanager.projects.get, container.clusters.get, ... 	Read-only access for devs

🔧 Create roles:

# Platform Admin
gcloud iam roles create sl_platform_admin \
  --organization=692154983500 \
  --title="SimpleLinks Platform Admin" \
  --description="Administers GKE and compute resources" \
  --permissions="compute.instances.list,compute.instances.get,container.clusters.get,container.clusters.list,iam.serviceAccounts.actAs" \
  --stage=GA

# Security Admin
gcloud iam roles create sl_security_admin \
  --organization=692154983500 \
  --title="SimpleLinks Security Admin" \
  --description="Manages security policies and audit logging" \
  --permissions="iam.roles.get,iam.roles.list,orgpolicy.policies.get,orgpolicy.policies.set,logging.logEntries.list" \
  --stage=GA

# Developer (read-only)
gcloud iam roles create sl_developer \
  --organization=692154983500 \
  --title="SimpleLinks Developer" \
  --description="Read-only access for developers" \
  --permissions="container.clusters.get,container.clusters.list,resourcemanager.projects.get,resourcemanager.projects.list" \
  --stage=GA

📝 Note: These are a starting point. You can add more permissions later with gcloud iam roles update.

